      "flags": {},
      "order": 16,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Full / Stitch Ready / Final Clip",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Output / Stitch\n**Full:** true bypass; keeps the complete decoded clip.  \n**Stitch Ready:** for intermediate clips; removes the tail after the effective handover cutoff.  \n**Final Clip:** removes only reused continuation head overlap and keeps the complete tail/final-keyframe landing. On Clip 1 there is no reused head, so it behaves like Full.\n\nFor rendered multi-clip concatenation, use `Stitch Ready` on every intermediate clip and `Final Clip` on the last continuation segment. Video and audio always use the same trim range.\n\n\nFor the smoothest final joins, use the **3-Clip Showcase** or the separate **04 — Stitch Saved Chain** workflow. Those use the retained full context for Safe Tail Bridge, a short context-aligned video blend and a 15 ms audio de-click crossfade instead of a hard concatenation.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "### Output / Stitch\n**Full:** true bypass; keeps the complete decoded clip.  \n**Stitch Ready:** for intermediate clips; removes the tail after the effective handover cutoff.  \n**Final Clip:** removes only reused continuation head overlap and keeps the complete tail/final-keyframe landing. On Clip 1 there is no reused head, so it behaves like Full.\n\nFor rendered multi-clip concatenation, use `Stitch Ready` on every intermediate clip and `Final Clip` on the last continuation segment. Video and audio always use the same trim range.\n\n\nFor the smoothest final joins, use the **3-Clip Showcase** or the separate **04 — Stitch Saved Chain** workflow. Those use the retained full context for Safe Tail Bridge, a short context-aligned video blend and a 15 ms audio de-click crossfade instead of a hard concatenation.\n"
      },
      "color": "#66511f",
      "bgcolor": "#8a6d28"
    },
